---
import PublicLayout from '../layouts/PublicLayout.astro';
---

<PublicLayout title="Screenplay clearance with a paper trail">
  <div class="lp">
    <section class="lp-hero" aria-labelledby="route-heading">
      <div class="lp-hero-copy">
        <p class="lp-eyebrow">
          <span class="lp-kicker-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>Screenplay clearance &middot; Open source &middot; Self-hosted
        </p>
        <h1 id="route-heading" tabindex="-1" class="lp-h1">
          Clear the script before it becomes a production problem.
        </h1>
        <p class="lp-sub">
          ClearCut finds brands, people, places, music, and other clearance concerns; brings
          flagged passages together with retained source evidence; and keeps the team&rsquo;s final
          call attached to the exact line. Open source and self-hosted &mdash; your scripts and
          evidence never leave your servers.
        </p>
        <div class="lp-ctas">
          <a class="button button-primary" href="/app/auth/sign-in">Explore the live demo</a>
          <a
            class="button button-secondary"
            href="https://github.com/clearcut"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
          >
            View on GitHub
          </a>
        </div>
        <dl class="lp-hero-proof" aria-label="What the sample project contains">
          <div><dt>10</dt><dd>clearance categories checked</dd></div>
          <div><dt>10</dt><dd>flagged passages, each with a source</dd></div>
          <div><dt>4</dt><dd>where the sources disagree</dd></div>
          <div><dt>1</dt><dd>blocked until it is fixed</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <p class="lp-micro">
          Pre-loaded with the fictional feature <strong>Borrowed Light</strong>. No account
          required; nothing leaves your browser. See the <a href="/features">ten clearance
          categories</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</PublicLayout>
